<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns/"
                  id="Definitions_Process_MergeManagerWatch" targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="merge-steward" name="Merge steward"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="user" name="User"/>
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_Process_MergeManagerWatch">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Process_MergeManagerWatch" name="Merge manager watch: wake, read the queue live, route" processRef="Process_MergeManagerWatch"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_MergeManagerWatch" name="Merge manager watch: wake, read the queue live, route" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>The loop run by the session that holds the merge-steward lane (actor merge-manager, skill merge-manager-watcher): elected, appointed, or holding it for its own PRs only. Each wake reads the open PRs, the runner queue, main's verdict and the PR owners live, acknowledges merge requests within the heartbeat, and routes to the train, a direct merge, runner relief, a saturation meta-merge or a stalled-agent takeover. Every merge waits for the owner's own OK, given in the merge manager's session as one card per batch (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Approvals, B). How a sibling finds or elects the merge manager and sends it a request is Process_MergeRequest.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_Process_MergeManagerWatch">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Steward" name="Merge steward" partitionElementRef="merge-steward">
        <bpmn:documentation>The merge manager: the one session holding the merge-steward lane, by the owner's word, by election, or for its own PRs only. Each wake it reads the open PRs, the runner queue, main's verdict and who owns each PR, acknowledges requests within the heartbeat, then routes to the process the queue needs or stays idle. It hands over explicitly when it stops; like any agent it may stall, and the siblings then re-elect.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Wake</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Read</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_Needed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Lapse</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Lapsed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_Route</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Relieve</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Meta</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_Green</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_NotGreen</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_Approved</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Card</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_Train</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Train</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Direct</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Stalled</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Done</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_MetaDone</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_StalledDone</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Idle</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Owner" name="Owner" partitionElementRef="user">
        <bpmn:documentation>Approves in the merge manager's session only, one card per batch. An approval given in a sibling's session does not authorise a merge.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Owner_Approve</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:task id="Owner_Approve" name="Approve the batch card">
      <bpmn:documentation>In the merge manager's session only: one card per batch, naming each PR, after its six lines were posted in that chat. An approval given in a sibling's session does not authorise a merge (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Approvals, B).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="interaction-modality"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_22</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Wake" name="Timer, PR event, request, main run, or sibling message">
      <bpmn:documentation>The sweep cadence, as a backstop: every 10-15 minutes while a P0 PR is in flight, every 30 minutes otherwise. Otherwise a subscribed PR event, a sibling's merge request, a main run finishing, or a sibling's message wakes it. Never a polling loop inside a turn.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:timerEventDefinition id="Timer_Wake"/>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Read" name="Read the queue, acknowledge requests">
      <bpmn:documentation>Read live, never from a stored copy: the open PRs (draft, head, mergeable, owed checks, open owner decisions), the queued and running runs with the age of the oldest, the latest main push run, and each PR owner's last push or comment. One sweep runs merge:watch over every repository it holds. Liveness duty: acknowledge each new merge request within holding.heartbeatMinutes, and post a heartbeat with each sweep, so siblings can tell a live merge manager from a stalled one.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="merge-manager-watcher"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_Needed" name="Still holding the lane?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Yes while the lane is needed (laneNeeded), or while this session manages only its own PRs. No when it stops: the condition no longer holds, or it hands over to a named session.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="merge-manager-watcher"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_19</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_20</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Lapse" name="Announce the hand-over or the lapse">
      <bpmn:documentation>Tell every sibling and the owner, and update the durable note: either the session that holds the lane now, or that the lane lapses and each session merges its own green PRs with the owner's approval, still sending the six-line merge request.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="merge-manager-watcher"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_20</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_21</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Lapsed" name="Lane released">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_21</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_Route" name="What does the queue need?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Saturated: queued runs are 60+ minutes old and nothing has landed, or the owner says the runners are full. Stalled: a PR owner has been silent for 2+ hours. Ready: a merge request is in, with green owed CI. Otherwise nothing.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_19</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_5</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Relieve" name="Relieve the runners">
      <bpmn:documentation>Enforce the pacing rule of continual-progress (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Cancel CI): close superseded or duplicate PRs, such as a re-pin whose commits another open PR already carries, and cancel their runs; cancel stale queued runs that never started, never a main push run that has started; ask the owners of P3 PRs to return them to draft.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="merge-manager-watcher"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_12</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Meta" name="Saturation meta-merge" calledElement="Process_SaturationMetaMerge">
      <bpmn:documentation>Offer the card and land only on the owner's tap.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_Green" name="All green per rule 1?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Every check run on the head SHA has finished, and anything pending blocks; wait for every tier, e2e included. The full tier ran (the No new failures judge, or every full test shard); a draft or fast-tier-only pass never counts. Every judge passes (owner ruling, 2026-11-07): an aggregate job covers only the parts it names, and each test shard's own no-new-failures table lists 0 new failures; with no judge, each check concluded success, skipped or neutral. A cancelled job counts only when a later run of the same workflow on the same head passed that job. merge:watch prints this verdict per PR.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="merge-manager-watcher"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_10</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_NotGreen" name="Not green yet">
      <bpmn:documentation>Do not merge. The next wake reads the checks again.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_11</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_Approved" name="Pre-approved?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Yes when the owner already said to merge this PR when green, so no second card is needed. Otherwise the request goes on the next batch card.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="merge-manager-watcher"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_13</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Card" name="Post the request in chat, then the batch card">
      <bpmn:documentation>The sibling's six lines go into the merge manager's chat first; a request with no rendered preview and no reason goes back to the sibling (owner ruling, 2026-11-07). Then one card per batch, naming each PR, in priority order: P0 main-red fixes and the re-pin chain, P1 work they unblock, P2 CI speed, P3 the rest.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="interaction-modality"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_Train" name="Rides the train?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Yes for a folio-assistant PR that does not change .github/workflows/. No for a workflow PR, or a PR in a repository with no train (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Train, A).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="merge-manager-watcher"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_22</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_17</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Train" name="Merge train" calledElement="Process_MergeTrain">
      <bpmn:documentation>Add the merge-train label instead of merging; the train lands the batch with one CI run.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Direct" name="Merge it through merge:guard">
      <bpmn:documentation>A workflow PR, or a PR in a repository with no train, merges directly. A workflow PR needs no approval beyond the batch card (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Workflow PRs, A).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="merge-manager-watcher"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_17</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_18</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Stalled" name="Stalled-agent triage" calledElement="Process_StalledAgentTriage">
      <bpmn:documentation>A PR owner who stalled: tell the owner, then take the stalled PR over.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Done" name="Wake handled">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_18</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_MetaDone" name="Wake handled">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_StalledDone" name="Wake handled">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_9</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Idle" name="Nothing to do">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_6</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="Start_Wake" targetRef="Task_Read"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" sourceRef="Task_Read" targetRef="Gw_Needed"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_19" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_Needed" targetRef="Gw_Route"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_20" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_Needed" targetRef="Task_Lapse"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_21" sourceRef="Task_Lapse" targetRef="End_Lapsed"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" name="Saturated" sourceRef="Gw_Route" targetRef="Task_Relieve"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_4" name="Ready" sourceRef="Gw_Route" targetRef="Gw_Green"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_5" name="Stalled" sourceRef="Gw_Route" targetRef="Call_Stalled"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_6" name="Nothing" sourceRef="Gw_Route" targetRef="End_Idle"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_12" sourceRef="Task_Relieve" targetRef="Call_Meta"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_7" sourceRef="Call_Meta" targetRef="End_MetaDone"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_9" sourceRef="Call_Stalled" targetRef="End_StalledDone"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_10" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_Green" targetRef="Gw_Approved"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_11" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_Green" targetRef="End_NotGreen"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_13" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_Approved" targetRef="Gw_Train"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_14" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_Approved" targetRef="Task_Card"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_15" sourceRef="Task_Card" targetRef="Owner_Approve"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_22" sourceRef="Owner_Approve" targetRef="Gw_Train"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_Train" targetRef="Call_Train"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_17" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_Train" targetRef="Task_Direct"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_8" sourceRef="Call_Train" targetRef="End_Done"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_18" sourceRef="Task_Direct" targetRef="End_Done"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_Process_MergeManagerWatch">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_Process_MergeManagerWatch" bpmnElement="Collaboration_Process_MergeManagerWatch">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Participant_Process_MergeManagerWatch" bpmnElement="Participant_Process_MergeManagerWatch" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="30" y="60" width="1270" height="860"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Steward" bpmnElement="Lane_Steward" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="60" y="60" width="1240" height="700"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Owner" bpmnElement="Lane_Owner" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="60" y="760" width="1240" height="160"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Start_Wake" bpmnElement="Start_Wake">
        <dc:Bounds x="132" y="412" width="36" height="36"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="90" y="452" width="120" height="53"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Read" bpmnElement="Task_Read">
        <dc:Bounds x="250" y="370" width="120" height="120"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Gw_Needed" bpmnElement="Gw_Needed" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="420" y="405" width="50" height="50"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="395" y="345" width="100" height="50"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Lapse" bpmnElement="Task_Lapse">
        <dc:Bounds x="385" y="520" width="120" height="120"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Lapsed" bpmnElement="End_Lapsed">
        <dc:Bounds x="427" y="672" width="36" height="36"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="405" y="712" width="80" height="20"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Gw_Route" bpmnElement="Gw_Route" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="560" y="405" width="50" height="50"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="492" y="462" width="80" height="50"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Relieve" bpmnElement="Task_Relieve">
        <dc:Bounds x="630" y="80" width="120" height="120"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Call_Meta" bpmnElement="Call_Meta">
        <dc:Bounds x="790" y="80" width="120" height="120"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_MetaDone" bpmnElement="End_MetaDone">
        <dc:Bounds x="950" y="122" width="36" height="36"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="928" y="162" width="80" height="20"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Call_Stalled" bpmnElement="Call_Stalled">
        <dc:Bounds x="630" y="220" width="120" height="120"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_StalledDone" bpmnElement="End_StalledDone">
        <dc:Bounds x="790" y="262" width="36" height="36"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="768" y="302" width="80" height="20"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Idle" bpmnElement="End_Idle">
        <dc:Bounds x="567" y="560" width="36" height="36"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="545" y="600" width="80" height="20"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Gw_Green" bpmnElement="Gw_Green" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="680" y="405" width="50" height="50"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="665" y="350" width="80" height="50"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_NotGreen" bpmnElement="End_NotGreen">
        <dc:Bounds x="687" y="560" width="36" height="36"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="665" y="600" width="80" height="36"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Gw_Approved" bpmnElement="Gw_Approved" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="800" y="405" width="50" height="50"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="785" y="350" width="80" height="50"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Card" bpmnElement="Task_Card">
        <dc:Bounds x="765" y="520" width="120" height="120"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Owner_Approve" bpmnElement="Owner_Approve">
        <dc:Bounds x="765" y="780" width="120" height="120"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Gw_Train" bpmnElement="Gw_Train" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="960" y="405" width="50" height="50"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="902" y="462" width="78" height="40"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Direct" bpmnElement="Task_Direct">
        <dc:Bounds x="925" y="220" width="120" height="120"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Call_Train" bpmnElement="Call_Train">
        <dc:Bounds x="1060" y="370" width="120" height="120"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Done" bpmnElement="End_Done">
        <dc:Bounds x="1232" y="412" width="36" height="36"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1210" y="452" width="80" height="20"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_1" bpmnElement="Flow_1">
        <di:waypoint x="168" y="430"/>
        <di:waypoint x="250" y="430"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_2" bpmnElement="Flow_2">
        <di:waypoint x="370" y="430"/>
        <di:waypoint x="420" y="430"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_19" bpmnElement="Flow_19">
        <di:waypoint x="470" y="430"/>
        <di:waypoint x="560" y="430"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="480" y="410" width="30" height="20"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_20" bpmnElement="Flow_20">
        <di:waypoint x="445" y="455"/>
        <di:waypoint x="445" y="520"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="450" y="470" width="30" height="20"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_21" bpmnElement="Flow_21">
        <di:waypoint x="445" y="640"/>
        <di:waypoint x="445" y="672"/>
